---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout title="Nanovision | Diff / Patch">
  <main class="pt-24 pb-16 min-h-screen bg-background">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6">Diff / Patch</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-muted-foreground mb-8">Focus your coverage analysis on the changes that matter.</p>

      <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
        <h3>Patch Coverage</h3>
        <p>
          When working on a pull request or a feature branch, you often only care about the coverage of the code you
          just wrote or modified. Nanovision can accept a unified diff (patch) file to filter the coverage report.
        </p>

        <h3>How to use</h3>
        <p>Generate a diff file using git:</p>
        <pre class="bg-secondary/50 p-4 rounded-md"><code>git diff main > my-changes.patch</code></pre>
        <p>Then pass it to Nanovision:</p>
        <pre class="bg-secondary/50 p-4 rounded-md"><code>nanovision -diff my-changes.patch ...</code></pre>

        <p>The resulting report will highlight coverage specifically for the lines changed in your patch.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
